  "question": {
    "text": "Two vertical poles <math><mi>A</mi><mi>L</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></math> of height <math><mn>4&nbsp;</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and <math><mn>16&nbsp;</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> respectively stand apart on a horizontal plane. If <math><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></math> be the feet of the poles and <math><mi>A</mi><mi>M</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi><mi>L</mi></math> intersect at <math><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then the height of <math><mi>P</mi></math> from the horizontal plane is equal to"
